WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:02.380
- [Narrator] Over the past decade,

00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:03.980
Chinese President Xi Jinping,

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:05.800
and Russian President Vladimir Putin

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:07.224
have become close.

00:00:07.224 --> 00:00:08.880
(beeping sound)
(cameras clicking)

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:11.251
They made pancakes together.

00:00:11.251 --> 00:00:12.600
(chef speaking in foreign language)

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:14.675
And toasted with vodka.

00:00:14.675 --> 00:00:15.700
(crowd clapping)

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:19.060
Xi even presented China's first
Friendship Medal to Putin.

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:22.060
- The alignment between the
two countries is getting closer

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:24.920
and some analysts would
say it's more close

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:28.130
than at any point in the past 60 years.

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:29.070
- [Narrator] But that relationship

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:31.510
is now getting tested
after Russia's invasion

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:33.360
of Ukraine, which has prompted the US

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:34.970
and its allies to drop a barrage

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:37.210
of sanctions against Moscow.

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:39.410
They included hitting
Russia's energy industry,

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:41.500
a major source of the country's income,

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.250
as well as unplugging the
world's 11th largest economy

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:46.480
from the global financial system.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:49.732
But China has taken a different position.

00:00:49.732 --> 00:00:52.750
(Wang speaking in foreign language)

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:54.510
- [Narrator] As Russia's
biggest trading partner,

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:55.760
China could provide the country

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:56.840
with much-needed help

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:59.598
by purchasing energy and
providing financial services

00:00:59.598 --> 00:01:01.873
but the friendship has limits.

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:04.640
One of the biggest hits to Russia

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:06.270
has been its energy sector.

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:08.530
It's the world's largest
natural gas exporter

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:11.370
and produces about 10% of the world's oil

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:15.103
and last year, total exports
reached about $240 billion.

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:17.490
So when Putin deployed troops

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:19.490
to breakaway regions of Ukraine,

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:22.000
the West tried to hit
Russia where it could hurt.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:23.060
- One of the responses

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:25.260
that the West has had to Russia's invasion

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:30.050
is to reexamine the energy
relationship it has with Russia.

00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:32.090
- [Narrator] One of the
biggest reexaminations

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:34.000
was the Nord Stream 2 project,

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.920
a newly built pipeline that was expected

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:38.120
to send 55 billion cubic meters

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:41.320
of natural gas from Russia
directly to Germany,

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:42.710
doubling the volume.

00:01:42.710 --> 00:01:45.653
Germany said it would halt
the $11 billion project.

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:49.780
And as Russia has continued
bombarding civilian areas

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:53.210
of Ukraine, the US took
action against Russian energy.

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:55.670
- We're banning all imports of Russian oil

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:57.560
and gas and energy.

00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:59.550
- [Narrator] The UK also
said it would phase out

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:00.920
Russian oil imports

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:04.190
while the EU said it's aiming
to cut some imports too.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:06.633
China could help fill some of the gaps.

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:09.597
A few weeks before Russia's invasion,

00:02:09.597 --> 00:02:11.500
Putin visited the Chinese president

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:13.090
ahead of the Winter Olympics.

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:13.923
During their meeting,

00:02:13.923 --> 00:02:16.220
Beijing agreed to buy 100 million tons

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:18.060
of crude oil from its neighbor.

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:20.790
- There was another agreement
between Russia and China

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:22.225
to construct a new pipeline

00:02:22.225 --> 00:02:25.160
that would send an additional
10 billion cubic meters

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:26.120
of natural gas.

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:26.953
- [Narrator] That's on top

00:02:26.953 --> 00:02:29.060
of an existing 1,800-mile pipeline

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:31.770
that's already sending
16 billion cubic meters

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:34.010
of natural gas per year to China.

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:36.360
But even with all the
planned pipelines running

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:37.450
at full capacity,

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:39.630
China's purchase would still fall short

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:41.270
of what the Nord Stream 2 pipeline

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:43.980
was expected to send each year to Germany.

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:45.350
And all of these Chinese projects

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:47.480
will take years to fully bear fruit.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:49.600
- The deals are significant in size

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.450
but they still don't amount

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:55.360
to any sort of immediate
economic lifeline for Russia.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:03:00.260
The new pipeline won't
be constructed until 2026

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:02.960
and even the crude oil deal,

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:05.493
that will stretch out over
the course of a decade.

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:08.570
- [Narrator] Energy hasn't
been the only sector hit

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:09.403
by the West.

00:03:09.403 --> 00:03:12.550
It's also been isolating
Russia's financial industry.

00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:14.440
The US and its allies said

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:16.350
they would remove seven Russian banks

00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:19.100
from the global financial
messaging system, SWIFT,

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:21.230
which is used by more than 11,000 banks

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:22.253
and other organizations

00:03:22.253 --> 00:03:25.400
in more than 200
countries and territories.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:27.420
And getting excluded means these banks

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:29.580
can't execute financial transactions,

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:32.880
meet obligations or receive
payments for exports,

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:34.940
practically disconnecting a large part

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:36.360
of Russia's economy.

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:38.320
But China could help out here too.

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:42.370
- There was speculation that
perhaps China's rival system,

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:44.910
the Cross-Border Interbank Payment System,

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:46.920
could provide something of a lifeline

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:49.000
to Russian banks.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:50.330
- [Narrator] However, the Chinese system

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:52.030
has its own limitations.

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:53.450
Last year, it handled an average

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:56.240
of just 13,000 transactions a day.

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:58.340
Although the comparison isn't exact,

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:01.640
SWIFT processed more than
40 million messages per day.

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:03.630
- China's system is teeny at the moment,

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:06.500
so analysts don't really
think that the Chinese system

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:09.810
is a viable alternative.

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:11.650
- [Narrator] Russian banks
could also face problems

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:13.250
with their credit cards.

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:14.770
Visa and Mastercard said

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:16.990
they're suspending
their Russia operations,

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:18.910
which practically blocks many Russians

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:22.030
from purchasing goods or
services outside the country.

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:22.980
To get around this,

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:24.750
several Russian banks
said they were working

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:26.670
on the possibility of issuing cards

00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:29.930
that used China's
state-owned UnionPay system.

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:32.140
These cards are accepted widely online

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:33.970
and in stores around the world

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:37.160
but switching to this new
system would also take time.

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:40.520
- There are ways for China
to help Russia economically

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:42.797
but every time China helps Russia,

00:04:42.797 --> 00:04:47.780
it risks provoking further
confrontation with the West.

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:49.330
- [Narrator] So far, China has been trying

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:51.280
to strike a delicate balance.

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:53.506
It has opposed the Western sanctions.

00:04:53.506 --> 00:04:57.090
(Wang speaking in foreign language)

00:04:57.090 --> 00:04:58.110
- [Narrator] But at the same time,

00:04:58.110 --> 00:04:59.710
it hasn't signaled that it would be ready

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:01.730
to backstop Russia's economy.

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:04.550
US officials said that
Russia has also asked China

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:05.890
for military equipment

00:05:05.890 --> 00:05:08.206
and the White House issued an warning.

00:05:08.206 --> 00:05:11.230
- Should they provide
military or other assistance,

00:05:11.230 --> 00:05:12.920
that of course violates sanctions

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:16.150
or supports the war effort,

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:18.970
that there will be
significant consequences.

00:05:18.970 --> 00:05:20.650
- [Narrator] The Chinese
Embassy in the US said

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:23.010
it has never heard of
such a request from Moscow

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:25.090
and China has earlier made vague pledges

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:28.355
to facilitate negotiations to end the war.

00:05:28.355 --> 00:05:32.688
(Wang speaking in foreign language)

00:05:39.029 --> 00:05:39.890
- The bottom line for China

00:05:39.890 --> 00:05:43.200
is to ensure its own strategic interest.

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:44.680
Beijing wants to keep Russia close

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:48.210
as a strategic collaborator
against the West

00:05:48.210 --> 00:05:51.240
but it's also having to
manage its own relationship

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:52.073
with the US and the West

00:05:52.073 --> 00:05:54.375
to keep that from going off the rails.

00:05:54.375 --> 00:05:56.410
(dramatic music)

